{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>With a high hand</b> — Three times in the Masorah: here, and the other two: in parashat Masei (Numbers 15:30 — 'and the soul that acts with a high hand'), in parashat Shelach regarding the spy (Numbers 14:8). Teaches that Micah's idol passed with them, as they expounded: 'and passed through the sea of Reeds' (Amos 5:7)."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The first additional occurrence is cited by its phrase והנפש אשר תעשה ביד רמה (Numbers 15:30); the second is identified only as 'in parashat Shelach regarding the spy,' referring to Numbers 14:8. The concluding Amos quotation reads ועבר בים צרה in the Hebrew, matching the rabbinic derashah on Amos 5:7; rendered literally as written."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:49.764574619Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}